      "writtenOn": "2020-11-17T12:43:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this logic is actually correct, because a network has no hope of satisfying a multilayer NRI if it can only satisfy a lower-priority request and the NRI is already satisfied by a network that satisfies a higher-priority request.\n\nI think the kind of logic you\u0027d need is :\n\n  for (...) {\n    if (isRequest \u0026\u0026 satisfies \u0026\u0026 (isSatisfyingRequest || score \u003c asValidated) {\n      return true\n    } else if (any NAI is satisfying request(request)) {\n      // If this request is satisfied, but this NAI can\u0027t beat it through the test\n      // above, then it\u0027s not needed for this request, because even being good enough\n      // for one of the lower-prio requests won\u0027t be good enough.\n      return false\n    }\n  }",
