      "writtenOn": "2020-11-18T18:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Jean for the detailed feedback. I spent a bit of time looking at the code with the above and I think we are ok. Here is what I am thinking.\n\nI am assuming that we are ordering the list for nri.mRequests starting with the highest priority and then working our way down. Let me know if that assumption is off but that\u0027s how I have been thinking about it (otherwise we\u0027ll need another mechanism to determine priority). \n\nThat said, if nai.satisfies(req) is true, then either of these will return true:\nnai.isSatisfyingRequest(req.requestId) ||  mSatisfier.getCurrentScore() \u003c nai.getCurrentScoreAsValidated()\n\nAs soon as that is the case, we return true and don\u0027t evaluate the lower priority requests therefore it doesn\u0027t appear that we\u0027ll run into the scenario you have above. In other words, it seems this code would only return true in the case where we have the appropriate mSatisfier and its corresponding req.\n\nLet me know if that makes sense or not. If not, can you maybe provide a particular example where we might run into this issue with the way we currently have the network preferences setup. i.e. would we have an issue with a multilayer request for [OEM_PAID, Unmetered, Default]?",
      "parentUuid": "66a323a3_edf37e50",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3554,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 3554,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "c7664df0c7f6247c6d092ac432a3e6d07593b9aa",
